-- title:
--   Formal smoothness of the special fibre of C[J/varpiₜ]
-- statement:
--   Arithmetic data. Let $q$ be a prime and $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$; let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and assume (`hι`) that there is a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = \exp(2\pi i/q)$. Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^{\times}$ be the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^{\times} \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^{\times}$, with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^{\times} \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^{\times}$, so $H_1$ consists of the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$ and modulo $\ell$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((t))$ given by [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, the $L$-subfield of $L((t))$ generated by the image, under the coefficientwise embedding [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of $\mathbb{Q}((t))$, of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ over $\mathbb{Q}$.
--
--   Coefficient ring. Let $A$ be a Henselian discrete valuation domain with algebraically closed residue field, equipped with an $L$-algebra structure making $L$ its fraction field, with $q \in \mathfrak m_A$ and with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, and let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with Laurent series [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), the $q$-expansion $t^{-1} \cdot \mathrm{jNumQ}$ of the modular invariant. Let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak m_A$, and let $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   Supersingular point and integral model. Write $C = \mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j$ for the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$. Let $y \subseteq C$ be a maximal ideal containing $\varpi$, and assume (`hss`) that every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from $C$ to an algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ with kernel $y$ sends $j$ into [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $j$-invariants all of whose elliptic curves over $\Omega$ have no nonzero $q$-torsion point. Let $X = \mathrm{AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel}\,A\,K\,j$, the pushout glueing $\operatorname{Spec} C$ to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the integral closure of $A[j^{-1}]$, let $z \in X$ be a point at which the germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ (taken along the structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$) lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal O_{X,z}$, and let $y'$ be a point of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ with `ιFin`-image $z$, satisfying the same supersingularity condition (`hss'`) and $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal} = y$.
--
--   Drinfeld-chart presentation of the completed stalk. Let $W_1$ be a complete discrete valuation domain, $\sigma_1 : A \to W_1$ a ring homomorphism with $\mathfrak m_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$, and $f_1, u_1, v_1 \in W_1[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u_1, v_1$ units and $f_1$ congruent to the Drinfeld form $X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$. Put $S = W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/\big(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v_1 - f_1u_1\big)$ with quotient map $\mathrm{mk}_S$, let $\mathrm{toC}$ be the map from $\mathcal O_{X,z}$ to its $\mathfrak m$-adic completion, let $\mathrm{germ}_Y : C \to \mathcal O_{X,z}$ be the canonical map from the finite chart algebra to the stalk, and let $e_1$ be a ring isomorphism from that completion onto $S$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hW₁` is a conjunction of seven clauses: (i) $e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC}$ carries the germ of each $a \in A$ to $\mathrm{mk}_S(C(\sigma_1 a))$; (ii) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ every $\tau \in \mathrm{Aut}_L(K)$ with [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) — i.e. $\tau$ acts on $q$-expansions by the substitution $\mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}$, in the sense that for all weights $k$, all modular forms $f,g$ of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions and $g \neq 0$, all $x \in K$ whose Laurent series is the ratio of those expansions, and all $\iota$ with $\iota(\zeta)=\exp(2\pi i/q)$, one has $\iota_*(\tau x)\cdot \mathrm{qExp}(g\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}) = \mathrm{qExp}(f\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1})$ — preserves $C$; (iii) if moreover $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod \ell$, such a $\tau$ fixes the point $y'$, namely $\tau(a) - a \in y'$ for all $a \in C$; (iv) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ as in (ii) preserving $C$ and fixing $y'$ in this sense, there exist a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c \in W_1$ and a matrix $M \in \mathrm{Mat}_2(W_1)$ such that $\theta$ is compatible with $\tau$ through $e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germ}_Y$, $\theta$ fixes the constants $\mathrm{mk}_S(C(w))$, $\theta(\mathrm{mk}_S X_j) \equiv \sum_i M_{ij}\,\mathrm{mk}_S X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by $\mathrm{mk}_S X_0, \mathrm{mk}_S X_1$, $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$ and $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak m_{W_1}$, $c \equiv 1$ modulo $\mathfrak m_{W_1}$ whenever $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod \ell$, and $c - 1 \notin \mathfrak m_{W_1}$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity; (v) for integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and primes $P_1,P_2$ of $S$, each not containing both $\mathrm{mk}_S X_0$ and $\mathrm{mk}_S X_1$, each containing $\mathrm{mk}_S(C(\sigma_1\varpi))$ and each containing an element $a_iX_0+b_iX_1+h$ with $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, if $q \nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$ then the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ to $\mathcal O_{X,z}$ along $e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC}$ are distinct; (vi) for a prime $P$ of $S$ not containing both $\mathrm{mk}_S X_0$ and $\mathrm{mk}_S X_1$, containing $\mathrm{mk}_S(C(\sigma_1\varpi))$ and containing some $X_0 + h$ with $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, an element $a \in C$ has $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germ}_Y a)$ in the contraction of $P$ along $e_1$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak m_A$; (vii) the series [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) (the image of the $j$-series `jqModC L` under the exponent scaling `qExpand L q`) lies in $K$ and in $C$, and there are $a_0 \in A$ with that element congruent to $a_0$ modulo $y'$, an integer $e_0 \ge 1$ and $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ such that the degree-$e_0$ form of $h$ takes unit values, namely $\sum_{i=0}^{e_0} \mathrm{coeff}_{X_0^iX_1^{e_0-i}}(h)\,a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit of $W_1$ whenever $a$ or $b$ is a unit and $a^qb-ab^q \in \mathfrak m_{W_1}$, and $e_1\big(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germ}_Y(\mathrm{jqNModC} - a_0))\big) = \mathrm{mk}_S(h)$.
--
--   Centre and blow-up chart. Let $J \subseteq C$ be the infimum of the set of ideals $J'$ for which there exist $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau \in \mathrm{Aut}_L(K)$ with `IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ` preserving $C$, such that $J'$ is the pullback along the restriction of $\tau$ to $C$ of the contraction, along $e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germ}_Y$, of the ideal of $S$ generated by $\mathrm{mk}_S(C(\sigma_1\varpi_t))$, $\mathrm{mk}_S X_0$ and $\mathrm{mk}_S X_1$. Let $B$ be the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ obtained by restricting scalars from the $C$-subalgebra generated by $\{x \in K : \exists\, i \in J,\ x\varpi_t = i\}$, that is $B = C[J/\varpi_t]$.
--
--   Conclusion. Under these hypotheses, the fibre `(IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A).Fiber B` of $B$ over the maximal ideal of $A$ is a formally smooth algebra over the residue field `(IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A).ResidueField`.
--
--   This is the local smoothness check for the weighted blow-up chart $C[J/\varpi_t]$ of the $j$-finite chart of the integral model of $X_{H_1}(q^2M')$ at a supersingular point whose completed local ring is presented by a Drinfeld-type equation $\varpi_t^{q+1}v_1 = f_1u_1$ with $f_1 \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$; the auxiliary level is cut out by the $\ell$-diamond condition, so that no lower bound on $q$ is imposed. It feeds the corresponding statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.formallySmooth_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.formallySmooth_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_of_dvd) about the blow-up chart itself.
